3. ASYMPTOTIC EXPONENTIAL RATES & DIRECT DIFFERENCE Delta_N
================================================================================
Testing whether D_0 and D_1 share a common leading exponential decay rate:
    alpha_0(N) = -log|D_0(N)| / N   vs.   alpha_1(N) = -log|D_1(N)| / N
and tracking the direct difference Delta_N = -log|D_0| + log|D_1|:
    If alpha_0 = alpha_1, the leading exponential factor cancels in D_0 / D_1.

